## Issue description
If I try to generate `fileSystems` mount point attributes dynamically, Nix bombs out with an "infinite recursion encountered" message.

### Steps to reproduce
Run `nixos-rebuild build` on this configuration:

    { config, lib, pkgs, ... }:
    with lib;
    {
      imports = [ /etc/nixos/hardware-configuration.nix ];

      # Create a user.
      users.users.sillyb = {
        isNormalUser = true;
      };

      # Try to dynamically generate mount points for the above user given a
      # list of directory names.
      fileSystems = let
        # Inputs.
        dirNames = [ "d1" "d2" ];

        # Helper function to make a mount point attribute out of a directory
        # name. Mounting each directory in our user's home.
        mountRoot = config.users.users.sillyb.home;
        mount = d: {
          "${mountRoot}/${d}" = {
            fsType = "vboxsf";
            device = "${d}";
          };
        };
      in
        # Generated mount points.
        foldl (ms: d: ms // (mount d)) {} dirNames;

    }

If it helps, this code used to work in 16.09.

## Technical details

* System: NixOS 17.03.873.0c041520c3 (Gorilla) running as a VirtualBox 5.1.14 guest)
* Nix version: nix-env (Nix) 1.11.8
* Nixpkgs version: 17.03.873.0c041520c3

**Describe the bug**
Example config
```
specialisation.gnome3 = {
  inheritParentConfig = true;
  configuration = {
    services.xserver.desktopManager = {
      pantheon.enable = lib.mkForce false;
      gnome3.enable = true;
    };
  };
};
```

gives me this [full traceback](https://gist.github.com/worldofpeace/2fdb54b73cd1b7bfebf899433f2c4332).

**To Reproduce**
Steps to reproduce the behavior:
1. Use `specialisation` your nixos-config while using nix flakes 
2. infinite recursion

**Additional context**
Code in nixos https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/f439dc71011a95d527ba115ea5a7b9764616b42b/nixos/modules/system/activation/top-level.nix#L151

**Describe the bug**
Under nixos-unstable, as of at most a couple days ago, overlays that used to work suddenly undergo infinite recursion.

**To Reproduce**
Steps to reproduce the behavior:
1. Try and build this shell

```nix
{ nixpkgs ? import <nixpkgs> {
  overlays =
    [
      (self: super: {
        haskellPackages = super.haskellPackages.extend(selfH: superH: rec {
          time-compat =
            super.haskellPackages.callCabal2nix
              "time-compat"
              (super.fetchFromGitHub
                {
                  owner = "phadej";
                  repo = "time-compat";
                  rev = "822e39074222ee01222c515a447c62a7df611ca3";
                  sha256 = "1di817ayj4xz43l3msahp8lxzf3slqmm8jdslcq6cik2m0ci962a";
                })
              {}
          ;
        });
      })
    ];
}
}:
nixpkgs.mkShell {
  buildInputs = [
    nixpkgs.haskellPackages.ghcide
  ];
}
```

**Expected behavior**
It used to work, and now it says infinite recursion. I'm not sure whether it was never supposed to work, but I don't think I'm doing anything wrong.

Works on nixos-20.03
Fails on nixos-unstable (as of recently)

I'm going to try and bisect the issue now.
